
ALGORITHM: Brute-Force String Matching

INPUT:
    Text T of length n
    Pattern P of length m

OUTPUT:
    Starting positions where P occurs in T
    Total character comparisons

1. Set comparisons = 0.
2. Set matches = an empty list.

3. FOR i = 0 TO n - m:
       Set j = 0.

       WHILE j < m:
           Increment comparisons.

           IF T[i + j] is not equal to P[j]:
               BREAK the WHILE loop.
           END IF

           Increment j.
       END WHILE

       IF j equals m:
           Add i to matches.
       END IF
   END FOR

4. Display matches and comparisons.
5. Return matches and comparisons.

END ALGORITHM
